---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import EnquiryForm from '../components/EnquiryForm.astro';
import MessageForm from '../components/MessageForm.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';

const pageUrl = `${SITE.url}/about/`;
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }];
const schema = [
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs, pageUrl),
  { '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': `${pageUrl}#page`, url: pageUrl, name: 'About SpaceToReno', about: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` } },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About SpaceToReno: Who Writes It and How It Works"
  description="Who runs SpaceToReno, how its renovation guides are researched and checked, how it links to its sister businesses, and how it handles your details."
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
      <span class="kicker">About</span>
      <h1>About SpaceToReno</h1>
      <p class="lede">A guide to renovating a home in Singapore: what to do, in what order, and what the rules say.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose prose-narrow">
      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        SpaceToReno is run by the team behind <a href="https://junktoclear.com.sg/">Junk to Clear</a>, a Singapore
        company established in 2009 under SKAP Waste Management Pte. Ltd. Junk to Clear handles clear-outs and
        disposal, and renovation work too. Its partner crews do the work, and Junk to Clear quotes, books and
        answers for each job.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same team runs sister sites: OurKampung, a guide to running your own home in Singapore, and
        services for moving, cleaning, repairs, aircon and pest control. A guide links to one of them only at
        the step that calls for it.
      </p>

      <h2>How we link to our own businesses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A guide links to Junk to Clear or a sister site only at a step that needs that service, such as getting quotes for the works or clearing a flat before hacking starts, and the sentence says it’s ours.</li>
        <li>A guide links to our own businesses at most twice.</li>
        <li>We never rank or review our own businesses against anyone else’s, and we don’t publish “best interior designer” or “best contractor” lists.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the guides are researched</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Rules come from the official source: HDB, BCA, URA, EMA, PUB, SCDF, NEA, the Consumers Association of Singapore (CASE) and Singapore Statutes Online. Each guide lists and links its sources.</li>
        <li>Where something depends on your condo’s by-laws or your contract rather than the law, we say so and tell you to check.</li>
        <li>We don’t publish prices, durations or statistics we can’t source. Where a guide talks about cost, it explains what drives it.</li>
        <li>Each guide shows the date it was last checked. Rules change, and if a source says something different from a guide, the source is right.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Guides are general information, not legal, engineering or financial advice.</p>

      <EnquiryForm
        id="enquiry"
        heading="Planning a renovation? Tell us about it"
        lede="Tell us about the home and the works. The team behind Junk to Clear, which handles renovations, will get back to you with a quote."
        pageName="About"
      />

      <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics.</strong> SpaceToReno uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which guides help
        people. It records the pages you view, how you arrived (from a search, for example), how far you scroll,
        which links to other sites you click, and your device, browser and approximate location. It uses
        first-party cookies to tell visits apart. It doesn’t collect your name or contact details. You can opt out
        on any site with <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google’s opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Enquiries.</strong> If you send an enquiry, the form sends what you enter (your property type,
        timing, the rooms or works, any details and budget range you add, your name and number) through FormSubmit,
        the form service we use, to the team behind Junk to Clear. They use it only to reply to your enquiry and
        arrange a quote, and don’t sell it. Google Analytics records that an enquiry was sent, not what was in it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Your rights.</strong> Under Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act you can ask to see or correct
        the details you sent us, or withdraw your consent to our using them. Use the form below and choose
        “A privacy request”.
      </p>

      <MessageForm />
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
